# ridge_watch
## The ridge
The ridge above the village is a long rock spine with a few twisted oaks on it, and a view of the whole of the north road for ten miles, a pale scar through the dark wood, going down to a bend and a stream and a very small stone bridge. It is the place where Sextus's sheep are folded in summer. It is the place where you stood, two years ago, and watched eleven grey cloaks make their camp.
Quintus has brought his goats up with him, as an excuse, and a horn made of a ram's horn that he has had since he was eight. He says that he will blow it once if he sees a lamp, twice if he sees more than ten, and not at all if it is only the moon.
?if b1.goat == "freed"
  "That one is the goat," he says, quite casually, of a stout, grey, evil looking animal. "It knows you. It has not forgotten."
?end
You set the watch together. Three boys on the ridge, two at the bridge, one on the oak by the well, a chain of horns and shouts that will carry a warning from the north road to the square in the time that it takes to count to forty. You make Quintus say it back to you.
$ _watch += 2
$ _prep += 1
$ bond.quintus += 3
:the_ridge
* Tell him that if he sees them, he is to come down at once, and not to try to be brave
  $ bond.quintus += 1
  $ humanity += 1
  He looks at you for a long moment. He says, with enormous dignity, that he is not a child. You say that you know. You say that it is exactly because he is not that you are asking. He looks away at the north road, and at the goats, and he swallows. "I will blow the horn," he says. "And I will come down. I promise."
* Tell him to blow it and stay, and that you will hold the road
  $ bond.quintus += 3
  $ defiance += 1
  His whole face lights up. It is a very bad thing to have done, and you know it as you say it, and you cannot make yourself take it back. He says "yes" with a grin like a fox's. You find that you are afraid for him in a way that you did not know that you could be.
-> :the_ridge_end
:the_ridge_end
