# aelia
## At the well
She has been waiting by the well for some time. She has her arms folded, and her chin up, and she has not been crying. She says, without any preamble, that her grandmother has told her not to ask, and that she has decided to ask anyway.
$ do meet("aelia")
She asks, "What are you?"
?if b1.farewell == "truth"
  You have told her once already, at the door, in a night of fire, in as few words as you could. You find that she remembers all of them.
?end
$ _aelia = 0
:the_answer
* Tell her the truth, all of it
  $ b1.aelia_talk = "truth"
  $ bond.aelia += 5
  $ secrecy -= 2
  $ humanity += 2
  You tell her. You do it badly. You do it in the order in which it happened, because you do not know any other, and you leave out the parts that you cannot say, and she listens with her mouth set and her eyes fixed on the water in the bucket. When you have finished she says that it is not as bad as she thought. She says that it is a good deal worse. She says that she does not think that she is afraid of you, and she does not know why that is. "You never stood still when you were alive, either," she says, and she laughs, once, very oddly.
* Tell her that there are things that you cannot say, and that you will tell her when she is older
  $ b1.aelia_talk = "kept"
  $ bond.aelia += 1
  She looks at you. She looks at you for a long time. She says, "That is what the grown ups say." Then she shrugs. It is a gesture of her mother's. "All right," she says. "But I will remember that you said it."
* Tell her that you are her father, or her mother, and that is enough
  $ b1.aelia_talk = "kept"
  $ bond.aelia += 2
  $ cunning_brutal -= 1
  She does not say anything. She puts her hand in yours, quite quickly, and takes it away again, as though she had been caught at something. "That is all I wanted," she says. "I only wanted somebody to say it."
-> :the_answer_end
:the_answer_end
She goes back to the house. At the corner she turns, and says, quite loudly, in the voice of a child who is making a point, that the thatch is wet, and the cisterns are full, and that she has been in charge of the hens.
$ _prep += 1
