# villa
## The villa
It is a long climb in the noon sun, up the old path through the oaks, with the white stone of the wall blinding on the ridge and the cicadas going like a thousand little saws. The sun lies on you, like a hand. You do not slow down. You have a great deal that you wish to do, and a limited time in which to do it.
$ do discover("the_villa")
The villa is as you left it. It is shut. The great gate hangs a little open, as it did on the first night, and the courtyard is full of dry leaves, and the fountain has a skin of green on it. The door to the cellar room is where it was. The bar is still on the inside. You stand in front of it for a long time with your hand flat on the wood, and it is not a thing that you can explain, even to yourself, why you do not go in.
?if b1.felt_below
  You think of a green bronze door in a cliff, behind a ring of backs. You think of a heartbeat that you did not mean to hear. It is, you find, a thing that does not leave you. It is as if the whole of the ground under Rome had a pulse, and you have been given, for the length of a few days, a very small ear.
?end
You make it ready. You sweep the leaves. You clear the cellar of its cobwebs and its wine jars, and you set a bench in it, and a barrel of water, and a pile of the old blankets from the upper rooms. It is a room with a stone vault and a door, and a bar on the inside, and a drain in the floor. It is the safest room for fifty miles, and nobody knows it, and that is, you think, very much the point.
$ _prep += 2
$ _watch += 1
:the_villa
* Bring the old and the small up here, at dusk, and bar the door
  $ b1.hill_ready = "some"
  $ _prep += 1
  It is a thing that you will have to ask of Domitia, who will not like it. It is a thing that you can see, as clear as a picture, the whole file of them going up the hill at the end of the day with blankets and bread, and the villa door closing, and the bar going down.
* Leave the cellar open, and tell them where it is
  $ _prep += 0
  You do not ask. You tell Sextus, and Sextus tells the shepherds, and it goes round. It will be used or it will not. It is not a thing that you can order.
-> :the_villa_end
:the_villa_end
